  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "stock-cdev-zero-initialization",
      "result": "CONFIRMED_STATICALLY",
      "details": "Ghidra stock zte_touch_probe allocates 0x1008 bytes with flags 0xdc0. In the mounted target kernel headers, GFP_KERNEL is 0xcc0 and __GFP_ZERO is 0x100 (___GFP_ZERO_BIT is bit 8); devm_kmalloc passes its gfp mask into the devres allocation. Thus the callback fields at +0xe18 and +0xee8 begin as zero in this initialization path."
    },
    {
      "id": "optional-callback-slots",
      "result": "NULL_GUARDED_AND_UNASSIGNED_IN_REVIEWED_STOCK_PATH",
      "details": "The stock Ghidra registration function assigns callback fields including +0xf98 and +0xfa0 but does not assign +0xe18 or +0xee8. Full stock assembly scan found exactly two accesses to those offsets and both are LDR instructions in tpfwupgrade_store and get_tp_noise_show; both functions guard the indirect call against NULL. No candidate C assignment to these slots was found."
    },
    {
      "id": "slot-lifetime-locking",
      "result": "CONSISTENT_STATIC_LOCK_ORDER",
      "details": "High-level fwimage, get_noise, FW_upgrade and self-test paths acquire tp_firmware_data_mutex before cmd_mutex where both are needed. tp_alloc_tp_firmware_data and tpd_copy_to_tp_firmware_data acquire cmd_mutex only and do not acquire the outer lock. The preserved stock call inventory shows tp_alloc is called only from tp_self_test_write; tpd_copy is called only from the three testing routines reached by tpd_test_cmd_store. The self-test write callback runs while the outer mutex is held, but releases cmd_mutex before calling the test callback, so the callback’s copy helper does not recursively acquire cmd_mutex."
    },
    {
      "id": "prior-vmalloc-retry-fixes",
      "result": "PRESENT_IN_CURRENT_SOURCE",
      "details": "Both allocation-failure paths clear descriptor slot +0xc58 before freeing the descriptor. The nine reviewed map entries remain HARDENED_STOCK_DEVIATION; this audit does not promote them to stock-exact."
    }
  ],
  "lock_order": "tp_firmware_data_mutex -> tpd_cdev+0xc60; no reverse acquisition in the reviewed paths",
